# Task Output Configuration

Controls where `/schedule` pushes confirmed tasks after saving to TASKS.md.
Edit this file to switch adapters or change target list/project settings.

---

## Plugin Root

<!--
  Auto-populated by /setup — do NOT hand-type this value.

  Why this exists: `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` is injected by Claude Code only into
  `command:`-type hook entries (hooks/hooks.json). It is NOT present in the
  Bash tool / osascript MCP environment that command prompts use to invoke
  scripts/cal_query.swift, scripts/match-delegate.ts, and the AppleScript
  adapters. Until that platform gap closes, commands resolve the install
  location via this field.

  /setup auto-detects the path on first install. Leave the placeholder below
  if you are reading this template manually — running /setup will replace it.
-->

plugin_root: YOUR_PLUGIN_INSTALL_PATH

---

## Active Adapter

reminders

---

## Done Archive

Controls auto-archiving of old Done records out of TASKS.md into
`TASKS-archive.md` (gitignored, lives next to TASKS.md). Issue #25.

done_archive_days: 30

Done records whose `Done:` date is strictly older than this many days
move to `TASKS-archive.md` on the next archive run. Records without a
parseable `Done:` date are kept in TASKS.md regardless of age (silent
drops would be worse than visible clutter).

Archival is opt-in per call site — issue #25 ships the `archiveOldDone()`
seam in `scripts/tasks-store.ts`; command migrations land in a follow-up.

---

## Session Briefing

Controls the SessionStart hook output (issue #22).

briefing_mode: full

Valid values:
- `full`   — always show the structured briefing (counts + triggered sections + suggested action)
- `quiet`  — collapse to a one-liner when no trigger fires; show the full briefing only when something needs attention
- `off`    — suppress the briefing entirely

The briefing is also rate-limited per day: once it has run today (recorded in
`memory/briefing-events.jsonl`), it will not show again until tomorrow.

---

## Adapter Settings

### reminders
list_name: YOUR_REMINDERS_LIST_NAME

### markdown-file
file: ./external-todo.md

### google
# Google Tasks adapter (#66). Set `Active Adapter` above to `google`
# to route /schedule and /today through this adapter. Shares the OAuth
# refresh-token lifecycle with the Google Calendar and Gmail adapters
# (issue #67); the same client_secret.json works for all three.
credentials_path: ~/.claude-eisenhower/google-client-secret.json
token_path:       ~/.claude-eisenhower/google-tasks-refresh-token.json
list_name:        Eisenhower List

### asana (future)
workspace_id: ~~asana_workspace
project_id:   ~~asana_project

### jira (future)
base_url:    ~~jira_url
project_key: ~~jira_project

### linear (future)
team_id:     ~~linear_team
project_id:  ~~linear_project

---

## How to Set Up

1. Copy this file: `cp task-output-config.md.example task-output-config.md`
2. Run `/setup` — it auto-detects the install location and rewrites the
   `plugin_root:` placeholder. Do not hand-type the path; the placeholder
   value `YOUR_PLUGIN_INSTALL_PATH` is intentionally invalid so a missing
   /setup run fails loudly the first time a script is invoked.
3. Set `list_name` under `### reminders` to the name of your Reminders list.
   It will be created automatically if it doesn't exist.
4. For the Google Tasks adapter (`Active Adapter: google`), fill in the
   `### google` block: `credentials_path` and `token_path` (gitignored;
   see `docs/CONNECTORS.md` for the Google Cloud Console OAuth client
   setup) plus `list_name` matching an existing Google Tasks list title.
5. The actual `task-output-config.md` is gitignored — never committed.

## How to Switch Adapters

1. Install the MCP connector for the new system via Cowork plugin settings
2. Create `adapters/[system].md` following the interface in `adapters/README.md`
3. Change `Active Adapter` above to the new adapter name (e.g., `asana`)
4. Fill in the adapter-specific settings under the matching `### [system]` block
5. No changes needed to `commands/schedule.md` or any skill files

See `adapters/README.md` for the full adapter contract.
